    icon: '🃏',
  },
  data: {
    LLM: "1. **Ante**: Every player contributes a fixed amount to the pot. 2. **Establish Trump**: A card is turned from the stock to name the trump suit. 3. **Participation**: Each player in turn decides to 'Play' or 'Fold'. Those who fold forfeit their ante. 4. **Tricks**: Active players play three tricks. Must follow suit; must trump if void; must over-trump if possible. 5. **Resolution**: The pot is divided into three parts. Each trick won awards one-third of the pot.",
    Player: "1. **Ante**: Every player contributes a fixed amount to the pot. 2. **Establish Trump**: A card is turned from the stock to name the trump suit. 3. **Participation**: Each player in turn decides to 'Play' or 'Fold'. Those who fold forfeit their ante. 4. **Tricks**: Active players play three tricks. Must follow suit; must trump if void; must over-trump if possible. 5. **Resolution**: The pot is divided into three parts. Each trick won awards one-third of the pot.",
    objective: 'Win at least one trick to earn a share of the pot and avoid the penalty of matching the pot.',
    gameplay: "1. **Ante**: Every player contributes a fixed amount to the pot. 2. **Establish Trump**: A card is turned from the stock to name the trump suit. 3. **Participation**: Each player in turn decides to 'Play' or 'Fold'. Those who fold forfeit their ante. 4. **Tricks**: Active players play three tricks. Must follow suit; must trump if void; must over-trump if possible. 5. **Resolution**: The pot is divided into three parts. Each trick won awards one-third of the pot.",
    keyRules: [
      "If you choose to Play and win 0 tricks, you must pay the 'Bestia' (match the current pot).",
      'The pot carries over if not all tricks are claimed (e.g., if some players fold).',
      'Winning the first trick confers the lead for the next.',
    ],
    bonusRuleGuids: [],
    useTrump: true,
    trumpBonusValues: null,
    setup: {
      players: '4 to 6 players; 5 is considered the ideal number for balanced play.',
      deck: 'A standard 40-card Italian deck (Swords, Batons, Cups, Coins). With Latin suits, ranks from high to low are: Ace, 3, King (Re), Horse (Cavallo), Jack (Fante), 7, 6, 5, 4, 2. When French suits are used, the Queen replaces the Horse.',
      equipment: 'Chips or currency for the central pot.',
      dealing: 'Deal 3 cards to each player (usually clockwise). One card is turned face up to determine the Trump suit.',
    },
    turnFlow: "1. **Ante**: Every player contributes a fixed amount to the pot. 2. **Establish Trump**: A card is turned from the stock to name the trump suit. 3. **Participation**: Each player in turn decides to 'Play' or 'Fold'. Those who fold forfeit their ante. 4. **Tricks**: Active players play three tricks. Must follow suit; must trump if void; must over-trump if possible. 5. **Resolution**: The pot is divided into three parts. Each trick won awards one-third of the pot.",
    moveValidityConditions: {
      ante: 'Mandatory for all players at the start of the round.',
      deal: 'The system automated dealer handles the distribution of three cards and the trump reveal.',
      reveal_market: 'There is no shared community market; the only public card is the trump proposal on top of the stock.',
      buy_market: 'Players cannot purchase or swap cards from any shared area in standard Italian Bestia.',
      buy_stock: 'The initial three cards are the only cards received; no buying from the stock is permitted during play.',
      fold: 'Allowed during the participation phase only.',
      check: 'The game uses a participation choice (Play or Fold) rather than a vying structure with checks.',
      call: 'There is no intermediate bet to match; competition is based on trick results and fixed penalties.',
      bet: 'Wagering is restricted to the initial ante and the potential penalty for taking zero tricks.',
      raise: 'There are no wagering rounds where players can increase the current value of the pot.',
      declare: 'Winning combinations are determined by trick capture rather than a formal declaration phase.',
      reveal_hand: 'Hands stay private until cards are played into tricks; no separate reveal phase occurs.',
      award_pot: 'Payouts are calculated and distributed by the system logic after the three tricks are completed.',
      play_card: 'Must follow suit; must trump if void; must over-trump if possible.',
      draw: 'Full hands are dealt at the start; no drawing phase exists during the play of the hand.',
      discard: 'Every card in the player hand must be played into a trick; no cards are discarded to a waste pile.',
      pass: 'Players must either choose to Play or Fold during the participation phase; they cannot simply pass.',
      bid: 'The trump suit is determined by a random flip from the deck rather than a bidding auction.',
      meld: 'Bestia is a trick-taking game based on single cards rather than forming sequences or melds.',
      go_out: 'The hand terminates for all active players simultaneously after the third trick is finished.',
    },
    exampleHands: [
      'Setup example: 3 card(s) per player.',
      'Rule example: Win at least one trick to earn a share of the pot and avoid the penalty of matching the pot.',
      "Turn-flow example: 1. **Ante**: Every player contributes a fixed amount to the pot. 2. **Establish Trump**: A card is turned from the stock to name the trump suit. 3. **Participation**: Each player in turn decides to 'Play' or 'Fold'. Those who fold forfeit their ante. 4. **Tricks**: Active players play three tricks. Must follow suit; must trump if void; must over-trump if possible. 5. **Resolution**: The pot is divided into three parts. Each trick won awards one-third of the pot.",
      'Scoring example: Zero-sum gambling chips. Highest net profit after a set number of deals..',
